#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""sf-system: the root helper of Seraphina OS Harness's Your server area (DESIGN.md section 42;
docs/seraphina/YOUR_SERVER.md section 6), phases P1a to P1c. It looks, and makes exactly two kinds of write, each in a
class the owner switches on himself: it refreshes Ubuntu's package lists (class "refresh", `apt-get update`, which
writes only /var/lib/apt/lists and runs apt's own hooks, as the daily timer does) and it adds names under the reserved
repository seraphina-keep/ to each app's current and previous image, so a clean-up never deletes them (class "keep";
it never removes a name or an image). Maintain, Fix and root-access changes (the design's P2 and P3) are not in this
program at all, and no request can reach them.

The owner installs a copy at /usr/local/libexec/seraphina/sf-system (root, 0755) with one paste that runs this
program's own `setup` mode through his own sudo; the sudoers file it writes lets Seraphina's own user run it with
no arguments at all. The request is one JSON line on standard input, at most 16 KiB:

    {"v": 1, "verb": "containers"}

and the answer one JSON line on standard output: {"ok": true, ...}, or {"ok": false, "error": "<code>", "words":
"<a plain sentence>"}. Exit 0: it answered; 2: it refused; 1: its own failure. Shaped exactly like bin/sf-snapraid
(the disk protection reader), except where the design's section 6.2 says otherwise: it knows its caller by uid
(SUDO_UID), answers only the uids its root-owned config names in `callers`, refuses every request from an account in
docker, lxd, incus-admin, disk or sudo (caller_holds_root: such an account needs no helper, and its agents would hold
root anyway), and refuses the class "private" (logs, who can act as root) to a person's login account
(caller_is_login_account), whatever its config says.

The verbs. Class "read": info, containers (Docker's state files, never the socket: Docker is never started), docker
(one of five read-only Docker API calls, only while docker.service runs and docker_api is on), compose (the name,
the service hashes and the image names Compose gives one folder, nothing else of its config), ports (who listens
where: process names and PIDs, never a command line), tailscale (each Tailscale container's names and serve entries,
decoded from three keys of its state file and nothing else), ingress (a login gateway's route table: listen, names,
paths, upstreams and whether a sign-in is asked; never header values, included files, certificates or keys), disks,
gpu, smart, needrestart, journal, du, job, log and receipts. Class "private": logs (one page of one app part's logs,
redacted here before it leaves root) and access (who can act as root, a job whose result stays here and is read a
page at a time). Class "refresh": apt.refresh (a job). Class "keep": keep.images. Every later verb (the P2 buttons and
the P3 access changes) is refused: "not_in_this_version".

Argument modes, for the owner's own sudo in a terminal (the harness's sudoers line allows none): `setup <staged
config>` (the one-paste install of section 6.11), `remove`, `explain helper-config` (what a staged .new config
allows, in this program's own words), `explain ingress` (the gateway's routes, for the owner's own check, lab L16) and
`explain access` (who can act as root, in this program's own words, before Seraphina has her own account). `run <job
id>` runs a job, only inside the transient unit this program started for it. `enrol`, `approve` and `confirm` belong
to later phases and are refused.

What it never does: no shell; no binary, path or config from the caller (every tool is at a fixed root-owned path
below, checked like this program's own file); no Docker call but the fixed list (DOCKER_CALLS) and no Docker command;
no container environment beyond seven named keys; no Cmd or Entrypoint; no Compose standard error (it can quote a line
of an env file); no Tailscale key but the three it decodes; no file of the gateway beyond its nginx config's route
fields; no log line that has not passed its own redactor; no install, removal, restart, upgrade, vacuum or clean-up;
no change to anything outside its own state folder, except the package lists (refresh), names under seraphina-keep/
(keep) and what `setup` and `remove` do with the owner's typed yes.

Standard library only; never imported by the harness at run time (the tests load it by path).
"""

